01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:02.000
as soon as the gas and the carburetor was gone.

01:13:02.420 --> 01:13:04.180
But why? Why did you do it?

01:13:04.480 --> 01:13:05.300
You had your question.

01:13:05.440 --> 01:13:07.820
Don't be technical. Why did you pretend to commit suicide?

01:13:11.840 --> 01:13:13.720
The car almost ran you down Saturday morning.

01:13:13.880 --> 01:13:15.420
You don't think that was an accident, do you?

01:13:16.480 --> 01:13:17.920
I couldn't get you to leave town,

01:13:17.960 --> 01:13:19.780
so I had to give him a different target.

01:13:20.570 --> 01:13:21.310
Different target?

01:13:21.530 --> 01:13:21.730
Me.

01:13:21.930 --> 01:13:25.800
A man doesn't kill my rose bush and my horse and my dog

01:13:25.800 --> 01:13:26.660
and then stop there.

01:13:26.820 --> 01:13:29.710
He must want to kill me.

01:13:31.530 --> 01:13:32.670
I can't wait any longer.

01:13:32.790 --> 01:13:36.560
Not while strange automobiles are trying to run you down on the highway.

01:13:37.470 --> 01:13:39.030
I've got to force his hand now.

01:13:39.990 --> 01:13:42.250
I want him to think that it's safe to take a shot at me.

01:13:42.350 --> 01:13:44.920
Do you understand?

01:13:46.670 --> 01:13:47.330
Not quite.

01:13:47.990 --> 01:13:49.710
I've tried to commit suicide, haven't I?

01:13:49.770 --> 01:13:52.700
It was on the radio. It says so right here.

01:13:53.990 --> 01:13:56.670
So what if somebody takes a shot at me now and leaves the gun in my hand?

01:13:57.300 --> 01:13:58.800
It's an open and shut case, isn't it?

01:13:58.840 --> 01:13:59.960
The police wouldn't even invest it.

01:14:01.790 --> 01:14:04.490
So he's free to kill me now if he can't.

01:14:05.940 --> 01:14:07.580
Doesn't have to hit around the edges anymore.

01:14:09.000 --> 01:14:10.380
But keep away from me.

01:14:10.480 --> 01:14:11.980
Don't stand too close to the target.

01:14:13.250 --> 01:14:15.190
Is that why you wanted me to leave Pinecliffe?

01:14:15.490 --> 01:14:17.490
That's why I want you to go home now and stay there.

01:14:18.600 --> 01:14:19.900
Lock the doors from the inside.

01:14:21.040 --> 01:14:23.500
If you have any visitors, don't let Aunt Amelia out of your sight.

01:14:24.310 --> 01:14:25.130
Don't trust anyone.

01:14:26.240 --> 01:14:27.860
Where will you be if I want to find you?

01:14:28.810 --> 01:14:29.970
I don't know, but I have to get...

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:35.800
out of here i can't wait for him to make the next move i've got to get out and go after him the

01:14:40.240 --> 01:14:57.550
exhibit was in 1929 the summer of 39 i ought to have that catalog somewhere here yeah and

01:14:57.900 --> 01:14:59.760
there's a list of all of the exhibitors in here

01:15:00.060 --> 01:15:00.940
The back of the booth.

01:15:01.160 --> 01:15:03.360
Practically every artist who might have known Torres.

01:15:04.870 --> 01:15:05.510
Oh, yeah.

01:15:06.660 --> 01:15:07.260
This is perfect.

01:15:07.480 --> 01:15:08.640
Exactly what I was looking for.

01:15:08.780 --> 01:15:09.020
Thank you.

01:15:13.610 --> 01:15:14.010
Good afternoon.

01:15:14.480 --> 01:15:14.740
Yes?

01:15:15.060 --> 01:15:15.980
Are you Mr. Strabini?

01:15:17.330 --> 01:15:18.410
Yes, that's me.

01:15:19.380 --> 01:15:22.100
Did you ever know an artist by the name of Vincente Torres?

01:15:22.600 --> 01:15:23.400
Vincente Torres?

01:15:23.720 --> 01:15:23.840
Yes.

01:15:24.270 --> 01:15:24.570
No.

01:15:37.930 --> 01:15:40.600
San Torres, certainly I knew him well.

01:15:41.420 --> 01:15:43.680
Watercolor man, no sense of death.

01:15:44.660 --> 01:15:47.960
Do you recall a painting he did, a portrait of an old woman with a guitar?

01:15:48.640 --> 01:15:50.420
An old woman with a guitar?

01:15:50.940 --> 01:15:52.280
Don't believe I was sorry.

01:16:06.360 --> 01:16:12.070
old woman with a guitar? Yes. I remember when Torres painted it. It was during his

01:16:12.070 --> 01:16:17.330
Renoir period. Do you remember who he sold it to? Didn't know he ever found a sucker.

01:16:17.690 --> 01:16:22.240
It was a piece of tripe. Well, thank you. Not at all.

01:16:43.380 --> 01:16:44.510
Hello, Sue.

01:16:45.320 --> 01:16:46.480
You've got a few phone calls.

01:16:47.630 --> 01:16:48.410
Anything important?

01:16:48.610 --> 01:16:49.550
I don't think so.

01:16:49.970 --> 01:16:51.430
A man named Carter called.

01:16:51.840 --> 01:16:53.740
He said he was a friend of an artist that you knew.

01:16:54.080 --> 01:16:55.540
The name sounded like Boris.

01:16:56.000 --> 01:16:56.640
Was it Taurus?

01:16:57.280 --> 01:16:57.720
Could be.

01:16:57.840 --> 01:16:58.480
Did he leave a number?

01:16:58.700 --> 01:16:58.900
No.

01:16:59.490 --> 01:16:59.970
He said it...

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:05.050
call back around 6. What's after that now? Well, Mr. Shepard's anxious to see you. He's still in the

01:17:05.050 --> 01:17:21.760
office. Shepard is safe. Oh, yes, just a minute. Carter. That's the man, Vincendi Torres. Do you

01:17:21.760 --> 01:17:29.740
remember a watercolor he painted a portrait of an old woman with a guitar? Do you remember who bought

01:17:29.740 --> 01:17:29.880
it?

01:17:30.800 --> 01:17:51.330
thank you just the man i've been looking for they wouldn't let me in the hospital and you

01:17:51.330 --> 01:17:58.690
seem to have disappeared since you got out some important things to do ben anyhow you're here now

01:17:59.000 --> 01:17:59.820
that's the main thing

01:18:01.500 --> 01:18:04.220
Of course I know it was an accident, boy, you couldn't have done it deliberately.

01:18:05.160 --> 01:18:05.640
Couldn't I?

01:18:06.710 --> 01:18:07.230
Of course not.

01:18:08.260 --> 01:18:09.860
Just the same, you've been overworked lately.

01:18:10.640 --> 01:18:11.660
Looking all fagged out.

01:18:12.000 --> 01:18:12.740
Time you took a rest.

01:18:14.500 --> 01:18:16.310
Yes, I could use a rest.

01:18:17.900 --> 01:18:18.880
Nice long rest.

01:18:20.000 --> 01:18:21.040
Just what I had in mind.

01:18:21.940 --> 01:18:23.480
Matter of fact, I'm tired myself.

01:18:24.070 --> 01:18:25.570
That's why I'm thinking of taking a trip.

01:18:26.280 --> 01:18:28.200
See something of the world before I get too old.

01:18:29.480 --> 01:18:29.980
Sounds like...

01:18:30.120 --> 01:18:31.060
Fine idea, Ben.

01:18:31.460 --> 01:18:33.080
A good idea for you, too, Jeff.

01:18:33.760 --> 01:18:34.680
Why don't you come along with me?

01:18:35.030 --> 01:18:36.450
Two of us could have a pleasant time together.

01:18:37.110 --> 01:18:39.650
Leave all our worries behind and take things easy for a while.

01:18:40.950 --> 01:18:43.390
What kind of a trip are you thinking of, Ben?

01:18:43.960 --> 01:18:45.260
I haven't made up my mind.

01:18:46.150 --> 01:18:46.910
Where would you like to go?

01:18:48.160 --> 01:18:51.560
Oh, an ocean voyage might be nice.

01:18:52.780 --> 01:18:56.800
If the ship had a low rail and a long drop to the water.

01:18:58.520 --> 01:18:59.900
Or Niagara Falls might be handy.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.220
or the top of the Empire State Building.

01:19:02.480 --> 01:19:03.600
Don't talk like that, Jeff.

01:19:03.760 --> 01:19:05.000
Don't even think of such things.

01:19:06.560 --> 01:19:10.210
I, uh, wasn't thinking of suicide, Ben.

01:19:10.390 --> 01:19:12.690
I don't expect to jump.

01:19:14.510 --> 01:19:15.430
I expect to be pushed.

01:19:16.880 --> 01:19:18.760
Jeff, you're talking like a paranoiac.

01:19:19.470 --> 01:19:20.570
Where did you get that word, Ben?

01:19:21.720 --> 01:19:24.000
Read it in a book, complete with all the symptoms?

01:19:24.660 --> 01:19:26.800
I'm only trying to help you, but if you're going to take this...

01:19:26.800 --> 01:19:29.910
Sit down, Ben. Sit down and listen.

01:19:32.970 --> 01:19:35.030
You had all the tools to work with, didn't you?

01:19:36.160 --> 01:19:39.750
Your ranch hands who think you're a king will do anything you tell them to.

01:19:41.000 --> 01:19:43.840
I was out your place yesterday, Ben, looking for Pedro.

01:19:44.790 --> 01:19:48.470
They told me he didn't work for you anymore, hadn't since the day after my house burned down.

01:19:49.950 --> 01:19:50.990
You let him go, didn't you?

01:19:52.240 --> 01:19:53.480
After he'd done his job.

01:19:56.020 --> 01:19:57.680
I'm beginning to think the doctor's right.

01:19:58.590 --> 01:19:59.910
I'm beginning to believe you do.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:07.510
have delusions of execution. Paranoia, Ben. You learned the word. Use it. When did you first plant

01:20:07.510 --> 01:20:14.140
the idea in Hartley's mind? Did you say, I'm a little worried about Jeff, and tap your finger on

01:20:14.140 --> 01:20:18.760
your forehead? Jeff, I'm not going to talk to you any longer. You're not in your right. Not while

01:20:18.760 --> 01:20:24.580
you're in your present mood. I'd do that if I were you. Haven't answered my questions, Ben. Are they

01:20:24.580 --> 01:20:28.100
too difficult? See if you can answer an easy one.

01:20:30.160 --> 01:20:32.540
Whatever happened to that painting that used to hang in your living room,

01:20:32.580 --> 01:20:35.490
the portrait of an old woman with a guitar?

01:20:36.600 --> 01:20:38.340
Wasn't in the living room, it was in my study.

01:20:41.340 --> 01:20:41.580
Why?

01:20:42.220 --> 01:20:43.100
When did you get rid of it, Ben?

01:20:44.470 --> 01:20:45.130
After it faded?

01:20:45.640 --> 01:20:47.760
After you found out what a sun lamp can do to a watercolor?

01:20:49.200 --> 01:20:50.680
Do you want to know who put me on your trail?

01:20:51.630 --> 01:20:52.370
You did yourself.

01:20:53.280 --> 01:20:55.740
When you tried to convince me I couldn't trust my memory anymore.

01:20:56.320 --> 01:20:59.430
I hate to say this, Jeff, but you can't trust your mind anymore.

01:20:59.660 --> 01:20:59.960
Can't I?

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:04.820
I made a written list the night I wrapped the hospital plans to make sure nothing was left out.

01:21:05.450 --> 01:21:08.630
And 17 blueprints were missing when the package was opened by the state board.

01:21:09.420 --> 01:21:11.220
No one could have tampered with that package but you.

01:21:11.340 --> 01:21:12.980
No one else knew it would be on my desk overnight.

01:21:13.300 --> 01:21:14.120
I didn't know any of them.

01:21:14.120 --> 01:21:15.140
Yes, you did. I told you.

01:21:16.220 --> 01:21:16.960
At the country club.

01:21:17.850 --> 01:21:20.130
You wanted to destroy my faith in my work, didn't you?

01:21:20.230 --> 01:21:22.320
It was the only thing I had left.

01:21:22.920 --> 01:21:24.490
Oh, Jeff, this is ridiculous.

01:21:24.830 --> 01:21:26.240
That's what I thought at the beginning.

01:21:26.800 --> 01:21:29.160
But once I began to suspect you, it all fitted together.

01:21:31.120 --> 01:21:35.060
I even remembered that your foreman was in the store the day I bought the can of gasoline.

01:21:36.500 --> 01:21:39.430
That gave you an idea, didn't it?

01:21:46.960 --> 01:21:47.560
An idea.

01:21:52.990 --> 01:21:57.940
How do you like waking up every morning wishing you were dead?

01:21:58.830 --> 01:21:59.710
You don't deny it anymore.

01:22:02.720 --> 01:22:10.280
No, you can't do anything about it.

01:22:11.470 --> 01:22:13.170
Go tell somebody I poisoned your dog.

01:22:13.690 --> 01:22:15.150
Go say I burned down your house.

01:22:17.670 --> 01:22:18.790
They'll think you're crazy.

01:22:19.600 --> 01:22:20.880
I don't care about the others.

01:22:20.880 --> 01:22:22.260
It's what you think that's important.

01:22:23.470 --> 01:22:24.890
You've been like a father to me, Ben.

01:22:26.240 --> 01:22:27.660
Funny kind of way you still are.

01:22:29.000 --> 01:22:29.740
What made you change?

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:31.260
What made you start to hate me?

01:22:32.070 --> 01:22:32.950
Was it Vivian?

01:22:33.790 --> 01:22:34.830
You killed her.

01:22:36.340 --> 01:22:38.800
I did everything for you that one man can do for another.

01:22:39.390 --> 01:22:40.590
And how did you repay me?

01:22:41.370 --> 01:22:42.390
You murdered her.

01:22:42.700 --> 01:22:43.820
Not murdered, Vivian.

01:22:43.900 --> 01:22:44.540
Not murdered.

01:22:44.680 --> 01:22:46.420
A drunken man at the wheel of an automobile.

01:22:47.280 --> 01:22:48.590
What is he if he isn't a murderer?

01:22:48.830 --> 01:22:49.410
Go in there.

01:22:50.640 --> 01:22:51.440
Go in there.

01:22:51.640 --> 01:22:51.780
Go.

01:22:51.980 --> 01:22:53.100
Alan, what do you do?

01:22:53.220 --> 01:22:53.460
Jeff.

01:22:55.700 --> 01:22:59.480
Mr. Shepard, this is Mr. Nelson, Fall River, Massachusetts.

01:23:00.410 --> 01:23:05.530
Last year, he was driving through California, and when he reached Pinecliff, he had an accident on 12-mile drive.

01:23:07.140 --> 01:23:10.040
Is this the man who was driving the car in which the girl was killed?

01:23:10.860 --> 01:23:15.540
Well, uh, you said not to say anything when you paid my damages.

01:23:23.770 --> 01:23:26.270
It wasn't. It was that fellow back there.

01:23:40.680 --> 01:23:46.680
Part of you gave the night before Vivian and I were to be married.

01:23:46.880 --> 01:23:49.260
I don't know whether you remember or not.

01:23:49.260 --> 01:23:52.580
I said something to you about those stuffy.

01:23:52.660 --> 01:23:54.280
I wanted to go outside for some air.

01:23:56.500 --> 01:23:57.720
Really looking for Vivian.

01:24:05.560 --> 01:24:06.520
I found her all right.

01:24:07.910 --> 01:24:09.230
I heard them talking to each other.

01:24:10.500 --> 01:24:11.700
It wasn't anything new, Ben.

01:24:12.600 --> 01:24:14.080
It had been going on for years.

01:24:14.630 --> 01:24:15.910
All the time I was overseas,

01:24:17.440 --> 01:24:19.280
he was telling her why he'd never marry her.

01:24:20.130 --> 01:24:20.710
He couldn't.

01:24:21.810 --> 01:24:23.090
Dodo wouldn't give him a divorce.

01:24:24.590 --> 01:24:27.720
So she said, run away without a divorce.

01:25:01.600 --> 01:25:03.720
I tried to catch him, but he was driving like a madman.

01:25:04.930 --> 01:25:07.330
We're coming to the port where a 12-mile drive meets the highway.

01:25:08.010 --> 01:25:09.990
I saw a car approaching on the main road.

01:25:10.930 --> 01:25:12.150
Ferris didn't see the other car.

01:25:13.020 --> 01:25:15.460
I knew what was coming, but there was nothing I could do to stop it.

01:25:15.880 --> 01:25:26.100
I jumped out of my car and ran toward the wreck.

01:25:35.980 --> 01:25:46.220
said do something do something for her nothing anyone could do for Vivian there's only one thing

01:25:46.220 --> 01:25:58.580
left to do for anybody I told him to take my car and get away from there find out how she died Ben

01:26:00.320 --> 01:26:28.770
what she was really like sorry you had to know that even now do you want I'm your little girl

01:26:30.410 --> 01:26:32.440
You're all I had after your mother ran away.

01:26:33.650 --> 01:26:34.250
She was...

01:26:34.250 --> 01:26:37.200
I never told you that, did I?

01:26:38.320 --> 01:26:39.780
Your mother was no good.

01:26:41.700 --> 01:26:42.600
You want to run away.

01:26:46.810 --> 01:26:47.070
Same.

01:26:49.220 --> 01:26:51.590
Jeff, I think so.

01:26:57.850 --> 01:26:58.210
See you.

01:27:00.250 --> 01:27:01.450
I'll kill both of them.

01:27:01.750 --> 01:27:08.680
Put down that gun.

01:27:08.860 --> 01:27:13.850
Put it down.

01:27:20.280 --> 01:27:21.360
You ran away from me.

01:27:24.940 --> 01:27:27.120
Well, you finally fixed me with the old man, didn't you?

01:27:28.230 --> 01:27:29.330
Never get any of his money.

01:27:29.470 --> 01:27:29.970
Now he's a...

01:27:30.120 --> 01:27:31.140
Nutty as a squirrel.

01:27:35.060 --> 01:27:35.860
Get out of here.

01:27:36.420 --> 01:27:37.380
Get out of Pinecliffe.

01:27:38.390 --> 01:27:40.220
If I ever see you again, I'll kill you.

01:27:40.960 --> 01:27:43.330
Dr. Hartley, this is Ellen Foster.

01:27:44.140 --> 01:27:46.320
Will you come over to Mr. Shepardopolis right away?

01:27:47.040 --> 01:27:48.260
Yes, yes, it's urgent.

01:27:49.280 --> 01:27:49.600
Thank you.

01:27:50.730 --> 01:27:51.510
It's all right, Ben.

01:27:53.160 --> 01:27:54.240
Everything's going to be all right.

01:28:01.920 --> 01:28:02.900
Well, doctor, will he live?

01:28:03.800 --> 01:28:04.820
He's healing beautifully.

01:28:05.460 --> 01:28:09.080
No infection, no complications, simple perforation of the deltoid.

01:28:09.340 --> 01:28:10.820
All the time I thought it was my shoulder.

01:28:11.400 --> 01:28:13.010
You won't need that thing anymore.

01:28:13.510 --> 01:28:13.810
Good.

01:28:14.550 --> 01:28:16.940
It'll be as good as new in a week.

01:28:17.350 --> 01:28:18.190
Tell me about Ben.

01:28:19.970 --> 01:28:23.460
Amelia, Ben was the psychopath, of course, from the beginning.

01:28:24.710 --> 01:28:26.210
I ought to have suspected it, of course.

01:28:27.760 --> 01:28:29.980
Now he's had what the psychiatrist...

01:28:30.060 --> 01:28:36.440
call a catharsis he's brought his troubles out into the open ellen helped to bring them out

01:28:36.440 --> 01:28:44.950
when she phoned fall river you'll be all right now in time well i'm very happy to hear that i hate

01:28:44.950 --> 01:28:51.100
to drag myself away but the ill and injured are waiting i'll see you to your car doctor bye ellen

01:28:51.100 --> 01:28:52.560
Jeff? Goodbye, Doctor.

01:28:52.680 --> 01:28:53.200
So long, Doc.

01:28:55.560 --> 01:28:56.400
Now, young lady,

01:28:58.720 --> 01:28:59.700
I suppose you'd come along with me.

01:29:17.180 --> 01:29:18.320
I've been wanting to ask you.

01:29:19.880 --> 01:29:20.420
Yes, Jeff?

01:29:22.180 --> 01:29:24.300
How in the world did you ever find that fellow from Fall River?

01:29:25.960 --> 01:29:29.980
Oh, found him in the traffic area.

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:31.580
and records at the police station.

01:29:33.530 --> 01:29:34.370
What made you think of him?

01:29:34.930 --> 01:29:36.110
The way you drove your car

01:29:36.110 --> 01:29:37.570
in 12-mile drive the other night.

01:29:38.340 --> 01:29:39.200
You could never have driven

01:29:39.200 --> 01:29:40.320
so recklessly with me

01:29:40.320 --> 01:29:41.100
if you'd been at the wheel

01:29:41.100 --> 01:29:42.120
when Vivian was killed.

01:29:42.980 --> 01:29:44.300
Not on the same road

01:29:44.300 --> 01:29:45.200
in the same place

01:29:45.200 --> 01:29:46.500
at the same time of night.

01:29:48.600 --> 01:29:49.180
Smart, aren't you?

01:29:49.640 --> 01:29:49.840
No.

01:29:50.160 --> 01:29:51.640
Yes, you are very smart.

01:29:51.880 --> 01:29:52.640
No, I'm not.

01:29:54.300 --> 01:29:56.150
I thought that you loved her.

01:29:56.420 --> 01:29:57.720
I thought you loved her all the time.

01:29:58.000 --> 01:29:58.980
I never really loved anyone.

01:30:00.700 --> 01:30:00.880
Thank you.
